Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 03:01:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 38/40] drm/imagination: apple: Report each VM's initial PM
 pool size

Pool-limit failures cannot be attributed without the sizes real scenes
ask the PM to hold. Log VM, blocks, clamp, tiles and initial free-list
pages once per VM when its first pool is built. Reuse existing values
and add no register access.

Affects: Apple A9 (S8003); A10 unchanged
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/pull/231#issuecomment-7138590680
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_apple_s8003.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_apple_s8003.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_apple_s8003.c
index 6a4affa..829487f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_apple_s8003.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_apple_s8003.c
@@ -256,6 +256,7 @@ struct s8003_vm {
 	u32 slot[2];			/* geometry and compute, fragment; 0: none */
 	u32 attached;			/* the firmware start the slots were loaded for */
 	struct s8003_pm pm[2];
+	bool pm_logged;			/* first pool sizing report for this VM */
 };
 
 struct pvr_apple_s8003 {
@@ -2159,6 +2160,13 @@ static int s8003_submit_geom(struct pvr_apple *apple, struct s8003_vm *vm, struc
 	blocks = max(DIV_ROUND_UP(hwrt->free_lists[0]->initial_num_pages, 32),
 		     DIV_ROUND_UP(50 + rt.tiles, 32));
 	err = s8003_pm_build(apple, vm, pm, min(blocks, S8003_PM_BLOCKS_MAX));
+	if (!err && !vm->pm_logged) {
+		dev_info(apple_dev(apple),
+			 "PM pool VM=%p blocks=%u clamped=%u tiles=%u initial_num_pages=%u\n",
+			 vm->vm_ctx, pm->blocks, blocks > S8003_PM_BLOCKS_MAX, rt.tiles,
+			 hwrt->free_lists[0]->initial_num_pages);
+		vm->pm_logged = true;
+	}
 	if (err)
 		return s8003_submit_error(apple, vm, "geometry", err, "PM pool build failed");
 	/* The record slot of the job before the last one is free again */
